          %h3#differentially Differentially
          %p
            In the literature this is usually discussed at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            level, hence for the corresponding
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"}> smooth functions
            +
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+fields"} Hamiltonian vector fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
          %p
            Now an (infinitesimal)
            %strong Hamiltonian action
            is a Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \colon \mathfrak{g} \to (C^\infty(X), \{-,-\})
            to the
            = succeed "-algebra:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
