                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \phi
            above, hence from the
            %em existence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonians"} Hamiltonians
            to an actual
            %em choice
            of Hamiltonians is in general not unique. In the literature the difference between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \phi
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            (or of their Lie theoretic analogs) is not always made clear.
