            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+representation"} projective
                Hamiltonian action:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+anomaly"} classical anomaly
          %h2#references References
          %p A comprehensive account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Viktor+Ginzburg"}> Viktor Ginzburg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Guillemin"} Victor Guillemin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yael+Karshon"} Yael Karshon
              %em Moment maps, cobordisms and Hamiltonian group actions
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://kolxo3.tiera.ru/M_Mathematics/MD_Geometry%20and%20topology/MDdg_Differential%20geometry/Ginzburg.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The perspective on Hamiltonian actions in terms of maps to extensions, infinitesimally and integrally, is made explicit in
          %ul
            %li#Brylinski
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              , Prop. 2.4.10 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
          %p
            The characterization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahBott
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"} Raoul Bott
              = succeed "," do
                %em The moment map and equivariant cohomology
              %strong 23
              1 (1984) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.math.sunysb.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Generalization to Hamiltonian actions by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            (instead of just a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
          %ul
            %li#Bos
              Rogier Bos,
              %em Geometric quantization of Hamiltonian actions of Lie algebroids and Lie groupoids
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.SG/0604027"}> arXiv:math.SG/0604027
              \&amp;rbrack;
